---
args: {"inquiry": "IntegrationInquiry", "atlas": "IntegrationAtlas | null"}
returns: "IntegrationBlueprint"
---
1. Bind prior = atlas when supplied, otherwise an empty IntegrationAtlas at revision zero with empty senses, bridges, handoffs, scenarios, waves, retainedOrganizationAliases and decisionHistory. Bind senses = readOrganizationalUsage(inquiry). Preserve source organization aliases and distinct senses under identical acronyms. Context-free glossary labels cannot establish equivalence.
2. For each plausible cross-organization sense pair bind bridge = testOperationalSubstitution(left, right, inquiry.usageSources). Collect bridges, retaining asymmetry, partial overlap and explicit team rejection. If a bridge is disputed, keep that operational boundary separate rather than forcing a universal definition.
3. For supported bridges bind handoffs = negotiateRoleInterfaces(bridges, senses, inquiry). Work at role level when personnel access is restricted. A similar job title or shared acronym is not a responsibility agreement.
4. Bind scenarios = walkCrossTeamTransactions(senses, bridges, handoffs, inquiry). Use their unowned steps and lost distinctions to revise the affected handoff proposals; no critical gap may disappear under a shared term.
5. Bind waves = planReversibleFamilies(bridges, handoffs, scenarios, inquiry, atlas). Any ambiguous meaning, unaccepted ownership, failed semantic round trip or missing exact integrity receipt holds that family. Independent ready families remain separate.
6. Bind nextAtlas: IntegrationAtlas = { revision: advance only when a sense, bridge, handoff, scenario or proposed wave changed; otherwise preserve prior.revision, senses: merge current source-backed senses by organization/context key while retaining prior aliases and evidence, bridges: append the newly tested bridge editions without deleting prior boundaries, handoffs: append current role agreements while retaining prior acceptances and rejected definitions, scenarios: append the current semantic rehearsals without overwriting prior editions, waves: preserve every prior wave with its effectiveDecisionAt and actualExecutionReceipt unchanged and append only newly planned, unexecuted family waves, retainedOrganizationAliases: union prior aliases with source-backed aliases from senses, decisionHistory: prior.decisionHistory unchanged because this program receives no migration approval or execution receipt }. Return { atlas: nextAtlas, readyWaveKeys: keys of waves whose round-trip, owner acceptance, integrity receipts and blockers are all resolved, disputedBoundaries: explicit non-equivalent, rejected or unresolved bridge boundaries, roleAgreements: handoff keys still requiring the identified owners' acceptance, sourceRequests: the smallest missing sources or integrity receipts }. Keep all disputed boundaries and smallest source requests visible; a planned wave is not an executed migration.
